BBUUGGSS
     Currently, aauu__ooppeenn() does not reserve kernel resources necessary to com‐
     mit the record to the trail; on systems supporting aauu__cclloossee(), the call
     will block until resources are available to commit the record.  However,
     this leads to the possibility of an action being permitted without the
     record being guaranteed to go to disk.  Ideally, aauu__ooppeenn() would reserve
     resources necessary to commit any submitted record, releasing them on
     aauu__cclloossee().

